      "side": 1,
      "message": "Table ref cleared when switching back\n\n`setTableRef` stores every callback, including the null Vue passes when the previous table unmounts. Tabs are patched in order, so moving from chassis 1 back to chassis 0 sets the new table and then overwrites it with null. clearSelectedRows, toggleSelectRow, and onChangeHeaderCheckbox all return immediately when the ref is missing, so row selection on that tab does nothing. The new tests only switch from index 0 to 1 (Sensors.spec.js 287–295), which is the direction that still works.\n\nIgnore the unmount callback:\n```\nfunction setTableRef(el: unknown) {\n  if (el) table.value \u003d el;\n}\n```\n\nPlease add a test that selects tab 1 and then tab 0 and asserts table is still set.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 190,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 195,
        "endChar": 1
      },
      "revId": "c5e096321e085a61d6f2c4a42fce11c24391bf2e",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2dfd0123_ad1841a9",
        "filename": "src/views/HardwareStatus/Sensors/Sensors.vue",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 225,
