      "writtenOn": "2026-10-30T17:21:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Selected tab index drifts from the chassis id\n\nactiveTabIndex changes only when the current chassis disappears. If a refetch inserts a chassis in front of the active one, or returns the collection in a different order, b-tabs stays on the old index while the table follows activeChassisId. Those are different panes, so the selected tab is empty. I reproduced this by selecting chassis 1 and then reversing the group list: activeChassisId stayed chassis1 and activeTabIndex stayed 1.\n\nKeep the index aligned with the id:\n```\nwatch(\n  sensorsByChassis,\n  (groups) \u003d\u003e {\n    if (!groups.length) return;\n    const index \u003d groups.findIndex(\n      (g) \u003d\u003e g.chassisId \u003d\u003d\u003d activeChassisId.value,\n    );\n    if (index \u003d\u003d\u003d -1) {\n      activeChassisId.value \u003d groups[0].chassisId;\n      activeTabIndex.value \u003d 0;\n      return;\n    }\n    activeTabIndex.value \u003d index;\n  },\n  { immediate: true },\n);\n```\nonTabChange already ignores an update whose chassis id did not change, so this resync does not clear the selection.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 211,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 225,
        "endChar": 0
      },
      "revId": "c5e096321e085a61d6f2c4a42fce11c24391bf2e",
